PageBeat is an original data-driven rhythm game in development, built in Unity with C#.

This repository is a public technical case study. The production source code, beatmaps, game content, artwork, audio and internal tooling remain private until launch.

PageBeat is being developed around responsive music timing, data-driven chart events, custom Unity Editor tooling and a performance-conscious runtime gamefield.

Key areas of work include:

Beat-synchronised gameplay timing and input judgement
Data-driven note, line, camera and visual-event systems
Custom Unity Editor workflows for internal beatmap authoring
Runtime pooling and preview optimisation for large beatmaps
UI systems, animation sequencing and scene transitions
Performance investigation and iterative profiling of the editor and gamefield
Technical evidence

This repository contains selected gameplay footage, annotated screenshots, architecture notes and engineering decisions from the project.

For independently written public source examples inspired by the types of engineering problems solved during development, see the PageBeat Engineering Showcase repository.

Technology

Unity · C# · Custom Editor Tooling · JSON Data Modelling · Git · Performance Profiling

